1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,586
A Zone operator picks a batch with one withdrawal and two user transactions and starts Sworn's local proof job:

2
00:00:08,636 --> 00:00:14,950
Tempo's code runs in a zero-knowledge VM, and the result goes to an auditor.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,167
Tempo's portal pays a withdrawal only after the Zone verifier accepts the batch,

4
00:00:21,217 --> 00:00:25,950
so everyone involved must be able to trust that check.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,617
The witness stays with the operator and the prover.

6
00:00:30,667 --> 00:00:36,320
Only hashes and counters reach Tempo: enough to check the proof,

7
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:39,950
not to see balances, senders or amounts.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,394
This is the Operator Console in a browser.

9
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:53,283
On a local workstation, the operator can start the real proof job for the supplied fixture.

10
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:58,283
It takes about fifteen minutes and sends no transaction.

11
00:00:58,333 --> 00:01:02,172
The evidence panel then reads Moderato live.

12
00:01:02,222 --> 00:01:06,617
Its pre-T13 prototype verifier accepts a malformed batch.

13
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:09,950
Sworn demonstrates the missing ZK check.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,063
Now Sworn, on a real batch from Tempo's integration tests: two user transactions and one withdrawal.

15
00:01:18,113 --> 00:01:25,668
Tempo's own batch verifier ran inside a zero-knowledge VM, and this contract checked the proof.

16
00:01:25,718 --> 00:01:28,711
Here it is on the explorer.

17
00:01:28,761 --> 00:01:31,753
Again, live: the real batch, true.

18
00:01:31,803 --> 00:01:35,809
Change one field, and it reverts: invalid proof.

19
00:01:35,859 --> 00:01:41,387
An equivalent malformed batch is accepted by Moderato's current prototype verifier,

20
00:01:41,437 --> 00:01:45,950
while Sworn rejects a mutation of its proven batch.

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:53,230
To be clear: this batch comes from a dev chain, not a Moderato Zone.

22
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:58,950
No portal uses it, and it does not protect withdrawals yet.

23
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,214
Sworn has no customers, revenue or payer agreement today.

24
00:02:04,264 --> 00:02:08,308
The first test is not broad adoption.

25
00:02:08,358 --> 00:02:14,158
A Zone business supplies a batch, its reviewer re-verifies it,

26
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:21,176
and we ask whether it needs the next batch or upgrade proved.

27
00:02:21,226 --> 00:02:25,856
Only then is Proof Operations a recurring service.

28
00:02:25,906 --> 00:02:29,950
Settlement integration remains a separate Tempo proposal.
